7 Oct, RHCSA Exam Question No 4

=======================================

Identity and Group Provisioning

user means to enter each user separately.

`groupadd -h` to see available options.
`useradd -h`
`which nologin` to see the full path of this command
`getent group` `getent passwd user`
`gpasswd -d user group` to remove a user from a group
If primary isn't mentioned, it means secondary.

What needs to be done:
Create a group named admins with a fixed GID of 3500
Create a group named users
Create accounts for the following: harry with a primary group of admins and a secondary group of users and a UID of 3455, natasha with secondary groups of admins and users and a UID of 3456, sarah with a non-interactive shell, and bruce who has a home explicitly and is a member of the admins group (Secondary group) (If they ask for this user to have a home directory, user -M)
Set all their passwords to "password"
Validate data
Test Sarahs nonlogin

Steps:
groupadd -g 3500 admins
groupadd users
useradd -g admins -G users -u 3455 harry
useradd -G admins,users -u 3456 natasha
useradd -s /usr/sbin/nologin sarah (check the path of nologin with which nologin, then enter the path after -s)
useradd -m -G admins bruce
There are multiple ways to set the password: 1) passwd user 2) echo "password" | passwd --stdin user
To validate: id user, getent group, getent passwd harry natasha sarah bruce, then pwck -r and grpck -r

To delete all this, just delete the user and the groups created.


Reasons why a user cant SSH, 1) User doesn't exist 2) Password isn't set 3) The account is locked